            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0537" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124a/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-17T11:00:00-05:00">December 17, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>117. Your 176, December 16, 11 a.m. I do not deem it necessary that this
                    Government reply to the question raised in the Liberian note which you
                    report.</p>
                <p>The substance of the Department’s note, quoted in its 115, December 11, 6 p.m.,
                    was communicated to the British, French, and German Governments.</p>
                <p>When is Dr. Smith sailing?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
